154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (The Sales Performance Analysis project was completed as part of the Alfido Tech Data Analytics Internship to examine retail sales data and identify key business trends. The analysis used the Superstore Sales Dataset, containing 9,800 sales records and 18 attributes related to orders, customers, products, regions, and transactions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
155 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (The main objective was to transform raw sales data into useful insights by analyzing monthly sales trends, regional performance, product categories, and customer purchasing patterns.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
156 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (The project began with data exploration using Python and Pandas. The dataset was reviewed for structure and quality, revealing 11 missing values in the Postal_Code column. The Order Date and Ship Date fields were converted into date formats to support time-based analysis.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (Exploratory analysis was conducted using visualizations such as Monthly Sales Trend, Sales by Region, and Sales by Category. These helped identify differences in sales performance across time, regions, and product categories.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (The findings show that some regions and categories contribute more significantly to total sales, while lower-performing areas offer opportunities for improvement. Monthly sales variations also highlight the importance of demand monitoring for inventory and promotional planning.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (Based on the results, the business can strengthen marketing in high-performing regions, improve weaker areas through targeted campaigns, and align inventory with high-demand categories. Overall, the project demonstrates how Python, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, and Jupyter Notebook can convert sales data into actionable insights for informed decision-making.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
